# Quizly frontend environment
# Next.js loads frontend/.env.local. This file is a reference/template.
# Copy it to .env.local only once; after that, switch modes by commenting
# or uncommenting the blocks below instead of copying files repeatedly.
#
# ========================== ONLINE MODE ==========================
# Active by default: local frontend uses the hosted Spring Boot backend.
NEXT_PUBLIC_EXAM_MODE=ONLINE
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://quiz-app-s033.onrender.com
ALLOWED_DEV_ORIGINS=localhost:3000
# AI proctoring microservice (set these to the deployed HTTPS/WSS URLs in production).
# Local development defaults for the Python service on port 8000:
# NEXT_PUBLIC_AI_PROCTORING_URL=http://localhost:8000
# NEXT_PUBLIC_AI_PROCTORING_WS_URL=ws://localhost:8000
#
# ============================ LAN MODE ============================
# To use the backend on your Wi-Fi/LAN:
# 1. Comment the three active ONLINE lines above.
# 2. Uncomment these three LAN lines.
# 3. Replace both IP addresses if your Wi-Fi assigns different addresses.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_EXAM_MODE=LAN
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://10.29.139.67:8080
# ALLOWED_DEV_ORIGINS=10.210.254.230:3000
#
# ========================== IMPORTANT ============================
# - Keep exactly ONE NEXT_PUBLIC_EXAM_MODE and ONE NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL active.
# - NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL is the Spring Boot backend's address.
# - ALLOWED_DEV_ORIGINS is the address used to open Next.js on the LAN.
#   Do not use 0.0.0.0 here; 0.0.0.0 is only the server bind address.
# - For a backend running on this same computer, use:
#     NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8080
#     ALLOWED_DEV_ORIGINS=localhost:3000
# - After changing .env.local, stop and restart the Next.js server.
#   For a production build, rebuild after changing NEXT_PUBLIC_* values.
